    {
      "id": "CTRL-R2-1",
      "status": "resolved",
      "prior_finding": "CTRL-R1-1",
      "finding": "Runner differs from preserved r1 only by g.copy() at prefix record creation. The independent consecutive-prefix replay exactly reproduces both corrected records after serialization. The first prefix no longer aliases the subsequently accumulated gradient.",
      "disposition": "Accept corrected check002 and charge_moment_checks_v2.json; retain original check001 and charge_moment_checks.json as invalid-gradient negative controls."
    },
    {
      "id": "CTRL-R2-2",
      "status": "verified",
      "finding": "Original source/report backups match the r1 review hashes; original charge and mixed receipts retain their hashes. Original and corrected compact receipts are byte-identical to their own run results. All 38 registered sources per run verify, using preserved r1 runner for check001; registered proof/binary/baseline identities and all nine observation prefix hashes per run verify.",
      "disposition": "Provenance preservation requirement satisfied."
    },
    {
      "id": "CTRL-R2-3",
      "status": "verified",
      "finding": "Correction changes exactly four earlier active-prefix gradient arrays and no other result fields. Recomputed serialized gradient closures and conditional-fit displacement errors support the report maxima. verify_receipts rejects exactly the four original aliased vectors and passes all nine corrected records; serialization_regression.json exactly matches these outcomes.",
      "disposition": "Finite saved identities now valid for the declared fixtures."
    },
    {
      "id": "CTRL-R2-4",
      "status": "verified_with_scope_limits",
      "finding": "check_mixed_term.py rebinds its cumulative response-gap array with np.maximum rather than mutating it in place, so it does not share the fixed aliasing defect. Projection random-grid check passes; stored mixed-term maxima agree with the report. Full tensor rows remain diagnostic only; no root training or estimator repair occurs.",
      "disposition": "Unchanged mixed-term numerical evidence accepted within its public-centre value-only scope."
    },
    {
      "id": "CTRL-R2-5",
      "status": "verified_with_scope_limits",
      "finding": "Report identifies the serialization defect, preserved originals, corrected receipt and regression. It explicitly restricts the fit identity to two unconstrained parameters with fixed nuisance values and no prior; identifies synthetic data, B=0 voltage witness, separately checked free response, and unresolved rank/conditioning extension. It distinguishes centre interpolation identities from derivative/uniform/physical coverage guarantees. Hypothetical factor and subtotal bytes are arithmetically consistent and exclude full target overhead.",
      "disposition": "Report accurately scopes the evidence; no additional source or documentation revision required."
    },
    {
      "id": "CTRL-R2-6",
      "status": "verified",
      "finding": "Corrected experiment README documents unused output paths, baseline prerequisites, archived invalid receipt, correct regression exit statuses, synthetic fixtures, B=0 and rank limitations. Compact registration copies are byte-identical to the three original run registrations. New root summary/state/handoff language preserves the same conditional scope.",
      "disposition": "Documentation and compact source bindings accepted. The additional architecture-gate and prior-artifact counts in validation.json are parent validation evidence and were not independently rerun in this review."
    }
  ],
